upstream #2744 (5151f19f3): a prompt chunk sends the tower only the images that end after
its start. prepare ran before every chunk, and when another prompt had taken the shared
image rows it re-encoded every image past the restore point, so images earlier chunks had
already injected went through the tower again on each switch. It now encodes from the
position it is given: the restore point before the first chunk, then each chunk's start.
A chunk's rows read no image ending by that start, and the rows are read through the
spans the encode writes, so a suffix lands where the chunks read it. Ownership unchanged.
PROVENANCE: ashhart/TensorFold commit 5151f19f3 (2026-11-10), main-only (post-v1.2.6);
applies clean against pristine v1.2.6 AND on the full 18-patch stack (verified in a
scratch clone of the tag). Host-side only: prompt_images.zig's prepare gains a from arg
(the restore point, then each chunk's start) + backend.zig's two call sites; no kernels,
no contract records. Upstream's own host tests ride in the patch. Value hypothesis: a
multi-image multi-turn prompt re-encodes less (their host test: 18 -> 12 tower passes);
opencode's screenshot-per-turn shape is the beneficiary. No knob: the behavior IS the
fix; the A/B flips by staging the patch list (the two-arm duel pattern).

